From: wu <wuc8974@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:46:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] feat(pqc-m6): keyring providers File / Env / Composite
 + OsKeyring stub

PQC migration (whitepaper 2.2.5 + 2.2.5.A): three sync keyring
implementations and a fail-closed stub for the future native keyring.
The store-side SyncWrappingKeyProvider surface (M5) is the contract; M6
delivers the providers that fulfil it.

- src/security/keyring-provider.ts:
  - encodeBase64UrlKey / decodeBase64UrlKey round-trip 32-byte keys
    through base64url; both reject non-Buffers and the wrong length.
  - generateWrappingKey produces 32 random bytes as base64url (8-call
    non-determinism check).
  - FileKeyring: POSIX mode 0600 / 0400 enforced at construction AND
    at every getActiveKey call; absolute paths only; symbolic links
    refused; cache keyed on mtime so a concurrent rewrite invalidates
    the read path; setShape() helper for tests and rotation.
  - EnvKeyring: re-reads process.env on every call (no cache), default
    per-keyId env var pattern is `${activeVar}__<keyId>` but a custom
    resolver can be injected.
  - CompositeKeyring: getActiveKey walks the providers in order,
    returning the first successful resolution; getKeyById walks all
    providers; both fail-closed with the last error surfaced.
  - createKeyring factory: a discriminated-union KeyringConfig
    (file | env | composite) drives recursive construction.
  - OsKeyring stub: throws with a "M6.B not implemented" message so a
    caller that pre-installs @napi-rs/keyring can swap in a real
    implementation without touching the store.
- src/security/keyring-provider.test.ts: 32 invariants - base64url
  codec, key generation, FileKeyring (mode/symlink/missing/active/
  primary override/cache invalidation/setShape/JSON parsing), EnvKeyring
  (no-cache re-read/missing-var rejection/per-keyId lookup), CompositeKeyring
  (first-success/walk-all/no-success rejection), createKeyring factory
  (recursive dispatch + unknown-kind rejection), and OsKeyring fail-closed.

